    fix: fill-in hints per placeholder slot + executed-ratio honesty in validate/history. Addresses LORE-050.
    
    Dogfood run 7 (scratch-dir validate --execute on gateway-drain-window
    from HEAD fdfcea5) measured 1/7 checks executed, 6/7 template-skipped,
    and the history record grading the class drifted_orders: [] — "not
    drifted" with no field saying 6/7 checks never ran.
    
    GAP A (placeholder fill-in guidance): new lore/placeholders.py — a
    per-slot-name hint table describing WHERE the value comes from (log
    path, health URL, env/config key name, board dir...), deployment-
    neutral by construction (no host paths, no URLs, no values, no secret
    material). Every surface that renders a check command now prints one
    `fill-in: <token> = <where-it-comes-from>` line per unfilled slot:
    runbook markdown (to_markdown), validate plan + --execute text output,
    consult --failure check lists. JSON contracts unchanged (to_dict pins
    hold, round-trip intact). Hint extraction scans the raw command
    (deliberately NOT quote-aware — a quoted '<key>' is still a slot the
    operator must fill; only the execution-side gate stays quote-aware).
    
    GAP B (executed-count honesty): LintReport gains derived
    executed_orders/not_executed_orders (from the closed outcome vocabulary:
    ok/error/timeout/unknown/env-absent executed; refused/absent/template
    never reached the runner — env-absent IS an execution, exit 127 is an
    answer about the machine). persist_validate_history records carry
    derived executed_count/total_checks; local_validation_note appends
    `; executed X/Y checks` to the consult/compile lint line when the
    record has the counts (pre-LORE-050 records render the old line
    byte-identically — no fabricated denominator). validate --execute text
    output prints `executed: X/Y checks` next to every verdict.
    
    Counts derived from SEED_CLASSES/outcomes everywhere, including tests
    (18 new tests in tests/test_lore050_placeholder_fill_in_and_executed_ratio.py;
    the LORE-045 record-shape pin widened to the new derived fields).
    
    Count-sync (LORE-029 convention, same commit): scripts/test-count.txt
    435->453; README/CONTRIBUTING/INSTALL/SKILL count literals resynced.
    
    Verified live end to end (scratch dir, gateway-drain-window):
    - validate --execute: executed: 2/7 checks; fill-in hints under each
      template check; record {executed_count: 2, total_checks: 7}.
    - consult: "...(local history, not operator attestation); executed 2/7
      checks"; consult --failure prints fill-in hints under each check.
    - Pre-050 record appended by hand: line shape unchanged, no ratio.
    
    uv run pytest -q = 453 passed; uv run ruff check . + ruff format
    --check clean; scripts/check-test-count.sh PASS.
